From e2ed02e1e41eec73183a6455ca807da6a1f625ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:53:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(api): HTTP API for the envelope engine, and a capacity
 qualifier on the site

Patch 0005. The engine gets a second surface. The CLI delivers engagements; the
API answers the website and any client integration. There is deliberately NO
TypeScript reimplementation of the constraints - two versions of the truth is
exactly what a provenance-first product cannot survive.

THE API (gridforge/api/, standard library only)

    python3 -m gridforge serve --port 8080
    docker build -t gridforge . && docker run -p 8080:8080 -e GRIDFORGE_API_KEYS=... gridforge

    GET  /health  /v1/version  /v1/platforms  /v1/intake/template
    POST /v1/qualify     seven fields -> binding constraint      (public)
    POST /v1/screen      full intake  -> screen payload          (key)
    POST /v1/study       full intake  -> model pack              (key)
    POST /v1/portfolio   [intakes]    -> ranked halls            (key)

- Zero dependencies, so the image is the interpreter plus the engine and there is
  nothing to patch. Threading server, per-IP token bucket, CORS allowlist, 512 kB
  body cap, structured errors, no stack traces to the caller.
- Fails closed: with GRIDFORGE_API_KEYS unset the paid endpoints refuse with 503
  rather than serving the deliverable for free.
- /v1/platforms returns what is deliberately ABSENT alongside what is present, so
  an integrator cannot quietly use a rack power the manufacturer never published.

THE COMMERCIAL GATE (gridforge/api/tiers.py)

The free tier has to be genuinely useful or nobody fills the form in, and must not
be the paid product or nobody pays. Public callers get the binding constraint and
why, racks as found and after relief, which item sets the date, and the list of
inputs nobody has measured. They never get capex, lead times, economics, the full
ladder or the scenario comparison - redacted server-side by key, at any depth. A
test asserts no currency figure can reach a public payload, and CI asserts it again
against the running binary.

THE SITE

- app/api/qualify/route.ts: validates with zod, calls the engine, persists to
  Supabase, returns the public payload. When the engine is unreachable it captures
  the enquiry and says so plainly - it never invents a number.
- components/CapacityQualifier.tsx + app/qualify: seven fields, then the binding
  constraint, the rack counts, what has to move in order, and the table of assumed
  inputs. Every figure comes back from the engine with an evidence class; nothing
  is computed in the browser.
- supabase/migrations/0002_qualifications.sql: every row is a real hall with real
  numbers. Over time that table is the proprietary asset the physics is not - the
  distribution of busway ratings, plant temperatures and contracted-versus-peak
  headroom across European halls. Nobody else is collecting it.
- Navbar gains one link; .env.example documents GRIDFORGE_API_URL / _API_KEY.

CI now also builds the site (tsc, lint, next build) and smoke-tests the running
API, including that the public payload leaks nothing priced and that a paid
endpoint refuses without a key.

106 Python tests pass, up from 84. tsc, next lint and next build are clean.
Also drops a stray intake.json that was committed to the repo root, and gitignores it.

